# local env files
#
# Ignore every .env variant and re-admit only the committed templates. The
# previous pair (`.env` + `.env*.local`) left everything else exposed —
# `.env.backup`, `.env.production`, `.env.staging` — each of which holds the
# same secrets as `.env`, so one `git add -A` was all it took.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

